      "The finite double-universal proof uses both actual context SHIFTs. The opening vector [free 0,free 1] and two specializations of the shifted double universal produce the reversed slot assignment [free 1,free 0]. The explicit typed 2\u21922 vector gives the exact raw swapVec0 bridge. No object axiom, GEN closure resource or shift-fixed context is assumed.",
      "The numerical client binds b at slot0 then a at slot1, matching the swap theorem. Coincident labels use implication identity; distinct labels use slot exchange. Actual numerical ALL and implication decoder conversions preserve all zero aliases and arbitrary decoded matrices, including the literal D0 with free label0. No freshness or closed-matrix restriction is hidden.",
      "The actual theorem holds for every \u03941 set-language theory T and all internal a,b,c in every I\u03a31 model. It does not require equality, Foundation, Choice or ZF axioms. ZF/ZFC audit clients are genuine specializations of that generic result.",
      "Template final changes only function-composition normalization and explicit output arity. Numerical final changes only the doubleBody 0+1+1/2 numeral coherence proof. One Template source failure and two numerical source failures are retained; successful logical contracts are unchanged.",
