  "review_markdown": "Final independent three-stage rho4 review: CLEAN.\n\nRead all196/55/85 source lines, the6/8+3/4+5/8 audits, guards and final proof deltas. Internal slot exchange preserves previous bound variables at every depth; double-generalization retains both shifted contexts with correct reversed opening. The numerical client uses identity for equal labels and decoder congruence for all numerical aliases. Arbitrary internal labels and matrices are covered with no axiom, object GEN, freshness, closed-matrix or standard-support premise.\n\nExact kernel evidence is Swap6/8/0warnings, Template3/4/ONE source warning and rho4 5/8/THREE source warnings; every audit has0warnings and only the standard three axioms. The Template normalization/arity repair and numerical two-slot numeral repair do not change the logical claims. Three nonpasses remain preserved.\n\nBound1877 comparisons across251 paths: all three fresh objects and42/45/102 input sets, exact10/11/38 project closures, six external boundaries, actual first Omega, compiler/pins, both Cantor artifacts, fifteen maintained files, six packaged plus three maintained unbuilt preflights, nine recorded rejects and all nine historical records/snapshots. Portable guards equal executed finals. Version queries in author preflights are distinct from proof builds. No reviewer compiler, checker/control replay or source edit occurred.\n\nThis logical-row checkpoint does not itself supply general internal proof transport or a PA/binary endpoint. Exact hashes, timings, warnings, placements and prior review packets are in child-independent-review.json; all original records remain unchanged.\n",
